# What never belongs in the image.
#
# The rule learned the expensive way on the baseball site: this file excluded
# `scripts`, and server.js imported from scripts/ to *read* its indices. The
# import threw, the throw was caught, the server logged "rebuilding from CSV",
# and every box score silently lost its scoring summary — live, with every route
# returning 200. So the default here is to copy, and each exclusion below says
# why it cannot be needed at runtime.

.git
.gitattributes
.github
node_modules

# Fetched sources. Gitignored anyway, so this is belt and braces — but they are
# 95MB and 388MB, they are input to `npm run build`, and nothing reads them at
# request time. data/indices and data/reference are NOT excluded: the server
# reads both on every boot.
data/sources

# The test suite runs in CI and locally, never in the container.
test

# Notes for people, not for the runtime.
CLAUDE.md
README.md
